be amended to provide that a person charged with an offense other than murder or treason is not entitled to bail if:\n(1) the proof is evident or the presumption strong; and\n(2) the state proves by clear and convincing evidence that no release conditions will reasonably protect the safety of any other person or the community.\n(This question concerns Article 1, Section 17 of the Constitution of the State of Indiana.)"},{"id":"in-clay-q-public-question-2","name":"Public Question #2","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Constitution of the State of Indiana be amended to permit the judge of a city or town court to reside in: (1) the county in which the court is located; or (2) the bordering county closest to the city or town in which the court is located? (This question concerns Article 6, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Indiana.)"},{"id":"in-clay-q-referendum-tax-levy-msd-of-shakamak","name":"Referendum Tax Levy MSD of Shakamak","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Metropolitan School District of Shakamak increase property taxes paid to the school corporation for no more than eight (8) years for the purpose of funding and maintaining daily educational operations, including recruiting and retaining teachers and staff, supporting essential safety initiatives, maintaining class sizes, and funding academic programs and opportunities to meet the learning needs of all students, in response to reductions in property tax revenue, by imposing a property tax rate that does not exceed $0.25 and results in a maximum annual amount that does not exceed $499,000. If this operating referendum public question is approved by the voters, for a median residence of $100,000, the property's annual property tax bill would increase by $81 per year."},{"id":"in-clay-q-court-of-appeals-judicial-retention-fourth-district","name":"Court of Appeals Judicial Retention - Fourth District","type":"Court Of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Judge Mary A. DeBoer be retained in office?"},{"id":"in-clay-q-court-of-appeals-judicial-retention-fifth-district","name":"Court of Appeals Judicial Retention - Fifth District","type":"Court Of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Judge Paul A. Felix be retained in office?"},{"id":"in-clay-q-retention-of-judge-of-the-indiana-tax-court","name":"Retention of Judge of the Indiana Tax Court","type":"Tax Court Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Judge Justin L. McAdam be retained in office?"}]}